{%- comment -%}
  Link to another instalment of a series, tolerating parts that are not
  published yet.

  Usage from a post body:
      include series_link.liquid part=4 text="part 4"

  The instalment is looked up by its `series_part` front matter instead of by
  file name. Jekyll's post_url tag aborts the whole build when the target file
  is missing, which makes it unusable while the later parts of a series are
  still unpublished drafts. This include falls back to plain text in that case,
  and the link appears by itself as soon as the part is committed.

  Note: Liquid parses tags even inside a comment block, so neither the usage
  example above nor the mention of post_url may be written with braces here --
  a post_url tag without a valid argument aborts the build at parse time.

  The series defaults to the Connect-4 search series and can be overridden with
  `series="..."`.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign series_name = include.series | default: 'connect4-search' -%}
{%- assign target = site.posts | where: 'series', series_name | where: 'series_part', include.part | first -%}
{%- if target -%}
  <a href="{{ target.url | relative_url }}">{{ include.text }}</a>
{%- else -%}
  {{- include.text -}}
{%- endif -%}
